Derived work: bounded stdio child + crash breaker
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream project : block/buzz
Upstream URL     : https://github.com/block/buzz
Upstream commit  : c5c4f39
Upstream license : Apache License, Version 2.0

The following files in this repository are derived from Buzz:

  crates/hq-desktop-core/src/stdio/child.rs
      derived from crates/buzz-acp/src/acp.rs
      (NDJSON line framing with a 10MB line cap, the bounded request /
      notification transport, the idle-vs-hard deadline read loop, and
      process-group teardown)

  crates/hq-desktop-core/src/stdio/circuit.rs
      derived from crates/buzz-acp/src/lib.rs
      (SlotCircuit / CrashVerdict crash breaker: 3 crashes in 60s open the
      circuit for 300s, jittered exponential respawn backoff, half-open probe)

Modifications made by Indigo AI:

  * Removed all Buzz-specific coupling: Nostr, the goose steer extension
    (`_goose/unstable/session/steer`), the usage tracker, the observer context,
    CODEX_CONFIG deep-merge, model-switch helpers, and persona plumbing.
  * Removed the Agent Client Protocol layer entirely (initialize, session/new,
    session/prompt, session/cancel, permission handling), leaving a
    protocol-agnostic NDJSON child that separate drivers build on.
  * Added a `StdioProcessRegistrar` seam so child processes join the host
    application's existing process registry and exit-drain path.
  * The child's stderr is piped and drained into the HQ diagnostic log rather
    than inherited (the host is a GUI application with no terminal, and an
    undrained stderr pipe deadlocks the child).
  * Replaced `tracing` with the HQ diagnostic logfile, and `nix` with `libc`
    for the process-group signal.
  * Added deterministic-time variants of the circuit-breaker transitions so
    breaker behaviour is testable without wall-clock sleeps.

